# ============================================================================
# CULT-ULHU map file: ruined_city
#
# FORMAT (wave 11 art pass). Line-based, UTF-8, '#' starts a comment.
#   map  <name>
#       Declares the map name. Must appear once, before any zone/place.
#   zone <name> <minx> <miny> <minz> <maxx> <maxy> <maxz> <ambientFear>
#       Rectangular region feeding world/ZoneDef (see src/world/Zone.h).
#       ambientFear is background fear 0..100. Zones may overlap; the engine
#       resolves zoneAt() in file order, so list specific zones first.
#   place <model> <x> <y> <z> <rotYdeg> <scale> <zone> [cull=<m>] [nevercull]
#       One prop instance. <model> is a repo-relative path to a .glb under
#       assets/world/<category>/<name>.glb (categories: terrain, buildings,
#       props, cult). <zone> must name a zone declared above. Optional
#       culling hints for the engine binding (wave 38): cull=<m> hides this
#       placement past <m> meters (overrides the model's lod rule);
#       nevercull pins it visible at any distance (hero landmarks).
#   lod <model> hide=<m> [low=<m>]
#       Per-model LOD distances for the engine binding (wave 38): the
#       engine may skip rendering past hide=<m> meters, and may swap to a
#       low-detail stand-in past low=<m> (low must be < hide; 0 = none).
#       One rule per model. Tuned from measured GLB triangle counts.
# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Anything else is a parse error
# (see src/world/MapLoader.h) reported with a line number.
#
# ART DIRECTION - ruined old city reclaimed by a newborn cult.
#   Palette: desaturated greys and cold stone blues for ruins; moss greens
#     creeping over rubble; ember oranges reserved for braziers and the
#     altar plaza (the only warm light in the scene); bone whites for the
#     skull piles and banners. Deep violet-black fog; night is the default.
#   Mood: a dead city that the cult is re-inhabiting. The old city reads
#     as abandonment (collapsed towers, colonnade fallen mid-row, rubble
#     choking the cross-streets); the cult base reads as occupation (tents
#     ringed around the altar plaza, banners on the approach road, braziers
#     lit, cages with occupants). The graveyard is older than the city.
#   Budget: this is the host-simulated build - keep every model < 5000
#     triangles, total map assets < 30 MB, ~100 placements.
#
# MODELS (reconciled 2026-10-07 with assets/world/MANIFEST.md): all paths
# below point at real CC0 (Kenney: Graveyard/Castle/Mini-Dungeon kits)
# downloads. Two provisional models had no equivalent in the packs and
# their placements were dropped: skull piles (4, cult base) and cages (5).
# Textures: each GLB references ../textures/colormap-<pack>.png.
# ============================================================================

map ruined_city

# zone: cult_base (ambient fear 62)
zone cult_base -60 0 235 60 0 365 62

# zone: graveyard (ambient fear 55)
zone graveyard -360 0 -80 -200 0 120 55

# zone: old_city (ambient fear 45)
zone old_city -220 0 -220 220 0 220 45

# zone: outskirts (ambient fear 28)
zone outskirts -500 0 -500 500 0 500 28

# --- wave 32: atmosphere (lighting/mood data for the UE5 binding) ---
# cult_base: your ground — cold violet dark, clear starfield, watchful
atmosphere cult_base fog=#0a0618,0.4 ambient=#241a3a,0.4 sky=#050214 stars=1.0
# graveyard: corpse-pale mist, stars guttering behind the haze
atmosphere graveyard fog=#101418,0.7 ambient=#1a2026,0.25 sky=#060a10 stars=0.3
# old_city: the drowned avenues — deep blue-black, heavy air
atmosphere old_city fog=#060a18,0.6 ambient=#141a30,0.3 sky=#030612 stars=0.6
# outskirts: thin dark, wind-scoured sky
atmosphere outskirts fog=#080714,0.35 ambient=#1e1630,0.35 sky=#040312 stars=0.95


# --- wave 38: LOD distances (hide = hide past this range in meters,
# low = switch to low-detail past this range; 0 = none) ---
# Tuned from measured GLB triangle counts: detail(<120) 150/60,
# props(<=450) 250/120, set pieces(<=900) 400/200, large 600/250,
# landmarks 900/300, ground fx 50-60, lit props 200-300.
# The engine binding consumes these (see unreal/Docs/SystemMapping.md).
lod assets/world/cult/altar-stone.glb hide=900 low=300
lod assets/world/cult/wood-structure.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/cult/fire-basket.glb hide=300 low=150
lod assets/world/cult/banner.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/buildings/stone-wall-damaged.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/buildings/tower-square-base.glb hide=900 low=300
lod assets/world/props/debris.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/buildings/stone-wall-column.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/buildings/wall-doorway.glb hide=400 low=200
lod assets/world/props/gravestone-cross.glb hide=250 low=120
lod assets/world/props/pine-crooked.glb hide=250 low=120

# -- cult base: the altar plaza --
place assets/world/cult/altar-stone.glb 0 0 300 0 1.5 cult_base nevercull
place assets/world/cult/wood-structure.glb -30 0 278 15 1.0 cult_base
place assets/world/cult/wood-structure.glb 30 0 278 55 1.0 cult_base
place assets/world/cult/wood-structure.glb -36 0 312 95 1.0 cult_base
place assets/world/cult/wood-structure.glb 36 0 312 135 1.0 cult_base
